00:05:43,333 --> 00:05:49,333
Some girls are out of this world

2
00:11:26,666 --> 00:11:32,666
How to Talk to Girls at Parties is a comedy, music,
romance film directed by John Cameron Mitchell.

3
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:16,000
In 1970s London, a teenage outsider named Enn falls in love with a
rebellious alien girl named Zan, who has come to Earth for a party.

4
00:22:53,333 --> 00:22:59,333
Together, they navigate the complexities of
intergalactic culture and the trials of first love.

5
00:28:36,666 --> 00:28:42,666
Zan, played by Elle Fanning.

6
00:34:20,000 --> 00:34:26,000
Enn, played by Alex Sharp.

7
00:40:03,333 --> 00:40:09,333
Boadicea, played by Nicole Kidman.

8
00:45:46,666 --> 00:45:52,666
PT Wain, played by Matt Lucas.

9
00:51:30,000 --> 00:51:36,000
PT Stella, played by Ruth Wilson.

10
00:57:13,333 --> 00:57:19,333
Vic, played by Abraham Lewis.

11
01:02:56,666 --> 01:03:02,666
How to Talk to Girls at Parties is a 2017 science fiction romantic comedy film directed by John Cameron Mitchell from a
screenplay he co-wrote with Philippa Goslett, based on the 2006 short story of the same name by Neil Gaiman.

12
01:08:40,000 --> 01:08:46,000
The film stars Elle Fanning, Alex Sharp, Ruth
Wilson, Matt Lucas and Nicole Kidman.

13
01:14:23,333 --> 01:14:29,333
Principal photography began on 9 November 2015 in Sheffield.

14
01:20:06,666 --> 01:20:12,666
The film had its world premiere at the Cannes Film Festival on 21 May 2017.

15
01:25:50,000 --> 01:25:56,000
It was released in the United Kingdom on 11 May 2018 by StudioCanal
UK and in the United States on 25 May 2018 by A24.

16
01:31:33,333 --> 01:31:39,333
The film explores themes of galaxy, london, england, 1970s, punk rock, alien.

17
01:37:16,666 --> 01:37:22,666
The tone is lighthearted and emotional and thought_provoking.
